IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part5`

-- Tests for wa-interpretation-part5.l4 (ss 33 to 39).  Expected values are written from the text.

§ `Tests -- Part V`

-- s 33: the repeal includes the provisions of other written laws that amended the repealed law, and only those.
#ASSERT `the provisions repealed along with a repealed written law` (LIST (`Provision of another written law` WITH `its citation` IS "Act A s 3", `it amended the repealed written law` IS TRUE), (`Provision of another written law` WITH `its citation` IS "Act B s 9", `it amended the repealed written law` IS FALSE), (`Provision of another written law` WITH `its citation` IS "Act C s 1", `it amended the repealed written law` IS TRUE)) EQUALS LIST "Act A s 3", "Act C s 1"
#ASSERT `the provisions repealed along with a repealed written law` (EMPTY) EQUALS EMPTY

-- s 34
#ASSERT `the repeal of a repealing enactment revives the enactment previously repealed` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the repeal of a repealing enactment revives the enactment previously repealed` FALSE)

-- s 35: the repealed enactment operates until the substituted provisions come into operation (beginning of that day, s 21)
#ASSERT `the repealed enactment remains in operation on` (Date 30 6 2025) `until the substituted provisions come into operation on` (Date 1 7 2025)
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed enactment remains in operation on` (Date 1 7 2025) `until the substituted provisions come into operation on` (Date 1 7 2025))
#ASSERT NOT (`the repealed enactment remains in operation on` (Date 2 7 2025) `until the substituted provisions come into operation on` (Date 1 7 2025))

-- s 36: each of the five kinds, both limbs
#ASSERT `the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `a district or other local division or area` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `a council, corporation, board, tribunal, commission, trust or other body constituted, or an election or appointment of its members` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `an office constituted or an appointment of an officer` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `subsidiary legislation, a warrant, a certificate or a document made` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `any other act, matter or thing` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `any other act, matter or thing` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the thing subsists and continues as if made or done under the repealing law` `any other act, matter or thing` FALSE TRUE)

-- s 37(1): the repeal does not affect any of (b) to (f); (a) does not revive; contrary intention -> not covered
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `reviving anything not in force or existing at the time the repeal takes effect` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `the previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything duly done or suffered under it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, before the repeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred before the repeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a penalty or forfeiture incurred or liable to be incurred for an offence committed against the repealed enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, interest, title, power, privilege, status, capacity, duty, obligation, liability, burden of proof, penalty or forfeiture` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e) is subject to The Criminal Code s 11 and the Sentencing Act 1995 s 10: not among the sources
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a penalty or forfeiture incurred or liable to be incurred for an offence committed against the repealed enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Criminal Code / Sentencing Act gate is about (e) only
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred before the repeal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a contrary intention appearing: the repealing law decides
#ASSERT `the repeal affects` `a right, interest, title, power or privilege created, acquired, accrued, established or exercisable, or a status or capacity existing, before the repeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- closing words
#ASSERT `it may still be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed or made` `a penalty or forfeiture incurred or liable to be incurred for an offence committed against the repealed enactment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it may still be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed or made` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, interest, title, power, privilege, status, capacity, duty, obligation, liability, burden of proof, penalty or forfeiture` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it may still be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed or made` `an investigation, legal proceeding or remedy in respect of any such right, interest, title, power, privilege, status, capacity, duty, obligation, liability, burden of proof, penalty or forfeiture` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it may still be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed or made` `a penalty or forfeiture incurred or liable to be incurred for an offence committed against the repealed enactment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `it may still be instituted, continued, enforced or imposed as if the repealing law had not been passed or made` `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred before the repeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- s 37(2)
#ASSERT `section 37 still operates` TRUE
#ASSERT `section 37 still operates` FALSE

-- s 38
#ASSERT `the subsidiary legislation continues in operation as if made under the repealing Act` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation continues in operation as if made under the repealing Act` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation continues in operation as if made under the repealing Act` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the subsidiary legislation continues in operation as if made under the repealing Act` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the continuing subsidiary legislation may be amended or repealed as if made under the repealing Act` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the continuing subsidiary legislation may be amended or repealed as if made under the repealing Act` FALSE)

-- s 39: expiry is treated as repeal for s 37
#ASSERT `the expiry or lapse of an enactment affects` `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred before the repeal` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the expiry or lapse of an enactment affects` `a duty, obligation, liability or burden of proof imposed, created or incurred before the repeal` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
